Haakon Studebaker <heptapod@yahoo.com> writes:
> I was wondering if I'm just having a false memory if this was true in 
> previous versions of Nethack.
> Did scrolls of remove curse ask the player what the player wanted to have 
> uncursed rather than having it done randomly?

There has never been anything random about an unconfused scroll of
remove curse. Prior to NetHack 3.0, it uncursed everything in
inventory (cursed everything if you were confused). With the
introduction of blessed non-weapon objects in 3.0, it was changed to
the current system of cursed scrolls not affecting anything, uncursed
affecting all worn/wielded items, and blessed affecting the whole
inventory, with affected objects being randomly cursed or blessed or
unchanged if you are confused. The only changes since then have been
refinements of what "worn/wielded" actually means, and prior to 3.1.0
blessorcurse() used to substitute blessings with curses if you were in
Gehennom.

(This is ignoring the unpunishment side-effect of the scroll, which has
remained pretty static.)

